692	doc.push(PB("Two test files were written without the house `@test` decorator and `main()` function. The runner imports each module and calls `main()`; these had none, so it printed the section header and **ran zero tests** — while the aggregate total rose from 326 to 340 on tests that had never executed. Two commit messages quoted the inflated numbers. It was caught by reading the per-file PASS count, not by the exit status: the suite said `340 passed, 0 failed`. Both files were rewritten in the house pattern and now run 15 and 15; the corrected total is 346."));
693	doc.push(PB("The rule the stage adds: **a new test file is verified by its own per-file PASS count, never by the suite total moving.** It is the same family as the vacuous ledger test, the self-referential ROI test and the inert guard — a green number that means less than it appears to. Four sessions, four different ways for a passing suite to be passing about nothing."));
