695	doc.push(H3("11.5 — Mutation testing, and the four guards the tests never covered"));
696	doc.push(PB("`assets/mutation-ingest-auth.py` applies eighteen mutations to the ingest gate and the key directory and records whether any test goes red. **Fourteen were killed. Four survived** — meaning the guard could be deleted and the suite would stay green. The four are M2 (the missing-token check, because no test sends a request with no `Authorization` header to an enrolled deployment), M3 (`resolve_token` raising inside the handler), M5 (a direct call to the route function bypassing the header check), and M9 (the `entry_hash` comparison, because the existing tamper test trips the `prev_hash` check instead)."));
697	doc.push(PB("These are test gaps, not code defects: the guards are present, they are simply not exercised in the way each mutation disables them. Each is written into the chat-7 carry-forward with the exact test to add, and a fix is verified by re-running the driver, which exits zero only when every mutation is killed. The driver keeps a pristine snapshot in `/tmp` and a `--restore` flag, because a run cut off mid-mutation leaves the tree modified and `git checkout --` has destroyed uncommitted work in this repository before."));
